1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,560
Under Mexico City
lies another city,

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,290
built on an
island in a lake.

3
00:00:05,330 --> 00:00:08,010
Around 1200 BC,
the Olmecs make

4
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:11,068
giant stone heads,
taller than a person.

5
00:00:11,108 --> 00:00:14,208
Around the year 200, the
great Pyramid of the Sun

6
00:00:14,248 --> 00:00:16,941
rises at Teotihuacan.

7
00:00:16,981 --> 00:00:19,881
In 1325, the Aztecs
build their capital,

8
00:00:19,921 --> 00:00:22,447
on an island in a lake.

9
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:28,356
In 1521, the Aztec capital
falls to Spanish forces.

10
00:00:28,396 --> 00:00:30,576
In 1810, Father
Hidalgo's call

11
00:00:30,616 --> 00:00:33,097
for independence rings out.

12
00:00:33,137 --> 00:00:35,257
In 1910,
a revolution begins,

13
00:00:35,297 --> 00:00:37,517
and lasts ten years.

14
00:00:37,557 --> 00:00:40,337
In the 1920s,
Diego Rivera paints

15
00:00:40,377 --> 00:00:43,443
giant murals of
Mexico's story.

16
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:46,303
Today, more than
130 million people

17
00:00:46,343 --> 00:00:48,440
call Mexico home.

18
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:52,260
Have you been to
Mexico? Tell us below.

